			<item>
				<title>The AI Agent Framework Landscape</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agent-frameworks/framework-landscape/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agent-frameworks/framework-landscape/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;simple-definition&#34;&gt;Simple definition&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#simple-definition&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;An &lt;strong&gt;agent framework&lt;/strong&gt; is a library or SDK that implements the plumbing every agent needs — the loop that calls the model, executes tools and feeds results back — plus state, memory, multi-agent coordination, human-in-the-loop, guardrails and tracing. You write the instructions, tools and business logic; the framework runs them.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>What Is an AI Agent?</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/what-is-an-agent/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/what-is-an-agent/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;simple-definition&#34;&gt;Simple definition&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#simple-definition&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;An &lt;strong&gt;AI agent&lt;/strong&gt; is a system where an LLM &lt;strong&gt;decides what to do next&lt;/strong&gt;, does it by &lt;strong&gt;calling tools&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;observes&lt;/strong&gt; the result, and &lt;strong&gt;repeats&lt;/strong&gt; until the goal is reached or it must stop.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A chatbot answers. An agent &lt;em&gt;acts&lt;/em&gt;: it can look up an order, check a policy, issue a refund, and email the customer — choosing the steps itself.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Python and TypeScript Agent Frameworks</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agent-frameworks/python-typescript-frameworks/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agent-frameworks/python-typescript-frameworks/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;how-to-read-this-page&#34;&gt;How to read this page&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#how-to-read-this-page&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Each profile answers the same questions: &lt;strong&gt;what is the core idea, what does minimal code look like, what is it good at, and what should you watch out for.&lt;/strong&gt; Code is deliberately minimal and uses a placeholder &lt;code&gt;MODEL&lt;/code&gt;; check each project&amp;rsquo;s documentation for current model identifiers and options.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Tool Calling (Function Calling)</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/tool-calling/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/tool-calling/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;simple-definition&#34;&gt;Simple definition&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#simple-definition&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tool calling&lt;/strong&gt; (also called function calling) lets an LLM ask &lt;em&gt;your application&lt;/em&gt; to run a function. You describe the available tools; the model replies with &amp;ldquo;call &lt;code&gt;get_order&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;{&amp;quot;orderId&amp;quot;: &amp;quot;8812&amp;quot;}&lt;/code&gt;&amp;rdquo;; your code runs it and sends the result back; the model continues.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Agent Frameworks for Java, Kotlin and .NET</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agent-frameworks/jvm-agent-frameworks/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agent-frameworks/jvm-agent-frameworks/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;why-jvm-native-agents-matter&#34;&gt;Why JVM-native agents matter&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#why-jvm-native-agents-matter&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Most enterprise systems of record — banking cores, insurance platforms, ERP integrations — run on the JVM or .NET. Building agents in the same stack reuses existing security (Spring Security, OAuth), transactions, data access, messaging, observability and deployment pipelines, and keeps agents close to the services they call. Since 2025 the JVM has gained a real choice of agent frameworks.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Model Context Protocol (MCP)</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/model-context-protocol/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/model-context-protocol/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;simple-definition&#34;&gt;Simple definition&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#simple-definition&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Model Context Protocol (MCP)&lt;/strong&gt; is an open standard for connecting AI applications to tools and data. An &lt;strong&gt;MCP server&lt;/strong&gt; exposes capabilities — tools to call, resources to read, prompt templates to use — and any &lt;strong&gt;MCP-compatible AI application&lt;/strong&gt; can discover and use them.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Agents with Spring AI: Tools, MCP and Memory</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/spring-ai-governance/spring-ai-tools-mcp-memory/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/spring-ai-governance/spring-ai-tools-mcp-memory/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;what-this-article-covers&#34;&gt;What this article covers&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#what-this-article-covers&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;How the agent concepts from Module 3 map to Spring AI 2.0 code:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;table-wrap&#34; tabindex=&#34;0&#34; role=&#34;region&#34; aria-label=&#34;Table&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Concept&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Spring AI&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Tool&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;@Tool&lt;/code&gt; method, &lt;code&gt;ToolCallback&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Identity passed to tools&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;ToolContext&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Agent loop&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Built-in tool execution in &lt;code&gt;ChatClient&lt;/code&gt;, or &lt;code&gt;ToolCallingAdvisor&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;MCP client&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;spring-ai-starter-mcp-client&lt;/code&gt; → tools as &lt;code&gt;ToolCallbackProvider&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;MCP server&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;spring-ai-starter-mcp-server-webmvc&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;@McpTool&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Short-term memory&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;ChatMemory&lt;/code&gt; + &lt;code&gt;MessageChatMemoryAdvisor&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Persistent memory&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;JdbcChatMemoryRepository&lt;/code&gt; (and Redis, Cassandra, Mongo, Neo4j)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;tools-with-tool&#34;&gt;Tools with @Tool&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#tools-with-tool&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-java&#34; data-lang=&#34;java&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nd&#34;&gt;@Component&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kd&#34;&gt;class&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&#34;nc&#34;&gt;OrderTools&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kd&#34;&gt;private&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;kd&#34;&gt;final&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;OrderService&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;orders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;OrderTools&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;OrderService&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;orders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;k&#34;&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;na&#34;&gt;orders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;orders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nd&#34;&gt;@Tool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;s&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;s&#34;&gt;        Get status, items and delivery estimate of one of the current customer&amp;#39;s orders.&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;s&#34;&gt;        Use when the customer asks where an order is. Order numbers look like A-12345.&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;OrderView&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nf&#34;&gt;getOrder&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nd&#34;&gt;@ToolParam&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;s&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Order number, e.g. A-12345&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;orderId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;                       &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;ToolContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;        &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;customerId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;na&#34;&gt;getContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;na&#34;&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;s&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;customerId&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;// from session, not the model&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;        &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;k&#34;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;orders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;na&#34;&gt;findForCustomer&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;orderId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;customerId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;                     &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;na&#34;&gt;orElseThrow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;-&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;k&#34;&gt;new&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;ToolException&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;s&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Order not found for this customer&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;));&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nd&#34;&gt;@Tool&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;description&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;s&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Refund an order of the current customer. Amount in EUR.&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;RefundResult&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;nf&#34;&gt;refund&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;orderId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;BigDecimal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;amount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;reason&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;ToolContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;        &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;customerId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;ctx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;na&#34;&gt;getContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;().&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;na&#34;&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;s&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;customerId&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;        &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;k&#34;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;orders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;na&#34;&gt;requestRefund&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;orderId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;customerId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;amount&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;reason&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;);&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;// limits enforced here&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-java&#34; data-lang=&#34;java&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;String&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;reply&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;chatClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;na&#34;&gt;prompt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;na&#34;&gt;user&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;customerMessage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;na&#34;&gt;tools&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;orderTools&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;na&#34;&gt;toolContext&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;Map&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;na&#34;&gt;of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;s&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;customerId&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;n&#34;&gt;authenticatedCustomerId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;))&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;na&#34;&gt;call&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;()&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;    &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;na&#34;&gt;content&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;();&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;w&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Spring AI generates JSON Schemas from method signatures; &lt;code&gt;@ToolParam&lt;/code&gt; adds descriptions and required flags.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;ToolContext&lt;/code&gt; passes data &lt;strong&gt;to the tool without sending it to the model&lt;/strong&gt; — use it for identity, tenant and correlation IDs.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;returnDirect = true&lt;/code&gt; on &lt;code&gt;@Tool&lt;/code&gt; returns the result to the caller without another model round trip.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Exceptions can be converted into messages for the model so it can recover; keep them short and helpful. (&lt;code&gt;ToolException&lt;/code&gt; above stands for your own exception type.)&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Enforce &lt;strong&gt;business limits in &lt;code&gt;OrderService&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, not in the prompt.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;the-tool-calling-loop&#34;&gt;The tool-calling loop&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#the-tool-calling-loop&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;figure class=&#34;diagram&#34; aria-label=&#34;How ChatClient executes tools&#34;&gt;&lt;figcaption class=&#34;diagram__title&#34;&gt;How ChatClient executes tools&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xA;  &lt;pre class=&#34;mermaid&#34;&gt;sequenceDiagram&#xA;    participant App as Your code&#xA;    participant CC as ChatClient&#xA;    participant LLM as ChatModel&#xA;    participant T as OrderTools&#xA;    App-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;CC: prompt + tools + toolContext&#xA;    CC-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;LLM: messages + tool definitions&#xA;    LLM--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;CC: tool call getOrder(A-10293)&#xA;    CC-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;T: getOrder(&amp;#34;A-10293&amp;#34;, ctx)&#xA;    T--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;CC: OrderView&#xA;    CC-&amp;gt;&amp;gt;LLM: messages + tool result&#xA;    LLM--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;CC: final text&#xA;    CC--&amp;gt;&amp;gt;App: content&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;By default the tool loop runs inside the model call. In Spring AI 2.0 you can instead add &lt;code&gt;ToolCallingAdvisor&lt;/code&gt;, which runs the loop &lt;strong&gt;inside the advisor chain&lt;/strong&gt;, so other advisors (logging, memory, guardrails, auditing) see every iteration — useful for agent observability and per-step policy checks.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Managed Agent Platforms and Low-Code Builders</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agent-frameworks/managed-agent-platforms/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agent-frameworks/managed-agent-platforms/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;simple-definition&#34;&gt;Simple definition&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#simple-definition&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;managed agent platform&lt;/strong&gt; runs agents for you. You bring agent code written with almost any framework; the platform provides an isolated, scalable &lt;strong&gt;runtime&lt;/strong&gt;, managed &lt;strong&gt;memory&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;identity&lt;/strong&gt; for agents, a &lt;strong&gt;tool gateway&lt;/strong&gt; that turns APIs into MCP tools, sandboxed &lt;strong&gt;browser&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;code&lt;/strong&gt; tools, and &lt;strong&gt;observability&lt;/strong&gt; — the operational layer most teams would otherwise build on Kubernetes.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Agentic Workflow Patterns</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/agentic-workflow-patterns/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/agentic-workflow-patterns/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;simple-definition&#34;&gt;Simple definition&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#simple-definition&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agentic patterns&lt;/strong&gt; are reusable shapes for combining LLM calls, tools and code — the &amp;ldquo;design patterns&amp;rdquo; of AI systems. Most production systems are a composition of a few of them. They range from fully code-controlled workflows to fully model-controlled agents.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>AI Security: OWASP LLM Top 10, Prompt Injection and Agent Security</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/spring-ai-governance/ai-security/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/spring-ai-governance/ai-security/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;simple-definition&#34;&gt;Simple definition&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#simple-definition&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI security&lt;/strong&gt; protects AI systems — models, prompts, data, tools and agents — from being manipulated, leaking information, or being used to cause harm. Classic application security still applies; LLMs add a new problem: &lt;strong&gt;instructions and data travel in the same channel&lt;/strong&gt; (natural language), so data can act like code.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Multi-Agent Systems</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/multi-agent-systems/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/multi-agent-systems/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;simple-definition&#34;&gt;Simple definition&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#simple-definition&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;multi-agent system&lt;/strong&gt; splits work among several agents, each with its own instructions, tools and context, which coordinate to reach a goal. It is the AI equivalent of a team: a lead delegates to specialists.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Agent Memory, State and Durable Execution</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/agent-memory-and-state/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/agent-memory-and-state/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;simple-definition&#34;&gt;Simple definition&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#simple-definition&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;LLMs are stateless: each call knows only what is in its prompt. &lt;strong&gt;Memory&lt;/strong&gt; is everything your system stores and feeds back so an agent can continue a conversation, remember a user&amp;rsquo;s preferences, learn from past cases, and resume a long task after a crash.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Agent Reliability, Guardrails and Evaluation</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/agent-reliability-and-evaluation/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/agent-reliability-and-evaluation/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;simple-definition&#34;&gt;Simple definition&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#simple-definition&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Agent reliability is the engineering that makes an agent do the right thing consistently, stop when it should, and fail safely when it cannot succeed. It combines &lt;strong&gt;guardrails&lt;/strong&gt; (prevent bad actions), &lt;strong&gt;budgets&lt;/strong&gt; (bound cost and time), &lt;strong&gt;evaluation&lt;/strong&gt; (measure behaviour before and after release) and &lt;strong&gt;observability&lt;/strong&gt; (see what happened).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>The Agent Protocol Stack: MCP, A2A, AG-UI, Agent Skills and AGENTS.md</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/agent-protocols/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/agent-protocols/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;simple-definition&#34;&gt;Simple definition&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#simple-definition&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Agents need to talk to three kinds of counterpart: &lt;strong&gt;tools and data&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;other agents&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;people through a user interface&lt;/strong&gt;. Since 2024 an open standard has emerged for each, plus two lightweight file conventions for giving agents know-how and instructions:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Agent Harnesses, Skills and Long-Running Agents</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/agent-harness-and-skills/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/agent-harness-and-skills/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;simple-definition&#34;&gt;Simple definition&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#simple-definition&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;An &lt;strong&gt;agent harness&lt;/strong&gt; is everything around the model that turns it into a working agent: the loop, tools, permissions, context management, memory files, sub-agents, skills, checkpoints and verification. Two agents using the same model can perform very differently because of their harnesses — which is why &amp;ldquo;harness engineering&amp;rdquo; became a discipline of its own in 2025–2026.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Computer-Use and Browser Agents</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/computer-use-agents/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/computer-use-agents/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;simple-definition&#34;&gt;Simple definition&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#simple-definition&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A &lt;strong&gt;computer-use agent&lt;/strong&gt; operates software the way a person does: it looks at the screen (screenshots or the page structure), decides what to click or type, performs the action, and repeats. &lt;strong&gt;Browser agents&lt;/strong&gt; are the web-only variant. They let agents work with applications that have no API.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Agent Identity and Access Control</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/agent-identity-and-access/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/agent-identity-and-access/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;simple-definition&#34;&gt;Simple definition&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#simple-definition&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agent identity and access control&lt;/strong&gt; answers three questions for every action an agent takes: &lt;strong&gt;who&lt;/strong&gt; is acting (the agent, the user, or both), &lt;strong&gt;what&lt;/strong&gt; are they allowed to do, and &lt;strong&gt;how&lt;/strong&gt; can we prove later what happened. Agents are a new kind of non-human identity that often act &lt;em&gt;on behalf of&lt;/em&gt; a human, so classic service-account thinking is not enough.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Agentic AI Strategy and Operating Model</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/agentic-ai-strategy/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/agentic-ai-strategy/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;simple-definition&#34;&gt;Simple definition&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#simple-definition&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;An &lt;strong&gt;agentic AI strategy&lt;/strong&gt; decides where agents should do work in the organisation, how much autonomy they get, what platform they run on, how value and risk are measured, and how people and processes change around them. It turns isolated pilots into a governed, scalable capability.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>System Design: Agentic Customer-Support Platform</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/case-study-support-agent/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/agentic-ai/case-study-support-agent/</guid>
